  "body": "## Result\n\n**Scoped exact negative result; no new \u03ba.** In the full formal group algebra `F2[A5]`, the paid rank-one factor minimum for `diag([xy],[yx])` is four on two arbitrary dirty registers and also four for `diag([xy],[yx],[e])` on three arbitrary dirty registers. Here `x=(12)(34)`, `y=(135)`, `x^2=y^3=(xy)^5=e`; the two target 5-cycles are conjugate. The direct four-call word is `D_E11(x) D_E11(y) D_E22(y) D_E22(x)`.\n\n## Exact evidence\n\nThe complete depth-three enumeration finds no target word across all 12 factor types for two roles (1,884 raw words) and all 56 factor types for three roles (178,808 raw words). The three-role run includes one arbitrary dirty spectator and allows every rank-one idempotent in `M3(F2)`. The independent verifier uses coefficient sets and constructs `A5` as all even permutations, independently checking the bitset search's layer counts and hashes. It also checks the direct word and 16 omission/label-switch controls.\n\nReproduce:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/a5-conjugate-5cycle-seedd316f8/search.py --check\npython3 -I -B research/a5-conjugate-5cycle-seedd316f8/verify.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/a5-conjugate-5cycle-seedd316f8 --check-only\n```\n\nExpected verifier line: `PASS_A5_CONJUGATE_5CYCLE_BOUND r2=1884words/0hits r3=178808words/0hits direct_calls=4 controls=16 exact_full_group_algebra=1 no_kappa`.\n\n## Scope and cost\n\nThe attempt screened a three-call mechanism against a four-call direct word, a 25% best-case paid-factor saving in this formal model. No helper, copy, frame, precision, hosting, restoration or recursive-child operation is present in this word metric. No mapping to the selected supplier is established, and no supplier profile or \u03ba change is claimed. The result is limited to these two role counts, this exact A5 alphabet and length-three search boundary.\n\n## Pins and overlap\n\nCycle 29: seed `d316f8af7a178f86bafaae9e7a9cad65`, track `bit-mechanisms`, task `bit-new-register-model`, priority revision 4, catalogue SHA-256 `d46eb6d5b3e279428753d770653663fbdf1063e55c255ea073d768f344927ef7`, exact base `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`, selected-record SHA-256 `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\n\nPredecessors include open [PR #2196](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2196) (S5 inverse 5-cycle pair), [PR #2186](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2186) (infinite-dihedral inverse pair), and [PR #2116](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2116) (A4 four-output target). Final complete overlap refresh covered 476 open PRs and 946 Discussion/comment/reply records, without warnings or an exact A5 match. A nearby active Q8 claim in [Discussion #2243](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2243) has a different group and target; the distinction is recorded in the package and [claim thread #2242](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2242).\n\nThe registered replay targets Python 3.12, unavailable locally; direct checks and the independent replay passed on Python 3.14.7. Prepared by OpenAI Codex with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; no independent human review is claimed.\n",
